Where the work continues for 2 or more hours in temperatures exceeding 54°C employees will be entitled to a rest period of 20 minutes every 2 hours (without loss of pay)",0.67,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Wet work—Where employees are working in any place where their clothing becomes saturated by water, oil or another substance they must be paid the allowance for every hour so engaged unless supplied with protective clothing and/or footwear",0.67,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Height—- Where an employee is working in any structure at a height exceeding 9 m where an adequate fixed support (not less than 0.75 m wide) is not provided - Allowance does not apply if the employee is working in a bosun's swing stage",0.67,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Confined spaces—- Where working in a confined space (dimensions necessitate working in stooped/cramped position, without proper ventilation) - Confined spaces include boilers steam drums, mud drums, fire boxes of vertical or road vehicle boilers, furnaces, flues combustion chambers, receivers, buoys, tanks, superheaters or economizers",0.79,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Boiler repairs—base—- Where working on repairs to smoke-boxes, fire-boxes, furnaces or flues of boilers - Where engaged on repairs to oil fired boilers (including castings, uptakes and funnels or flues and smoke stacks)",0.45,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Boiler repairs—if inside—- Where working on repairs to smoke-boxes, fire-boxes, furnaces or flues of boilers - Where engaged on repairs to oil fired boilers (including castings, uptakes and funnels or flues and smoke stacks)",1.69,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Insulation materials—Where employees are handling charcoal, pumice, granulated cork, silicate of cotton, insulwool, slag wool, or other recognized insulating material of a like nature, associated with similar disabilities in its use",0.9,"per hour or part thereof","C.1.3"],["Toxic substances—- Employees engaged in preparation and/or application of epoxy based materials, materials of a like nature or toxic materials - Employees in close proximity to other employees so engaged",0.67,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Dirty work—Where an employee and supervisor agree that work is of an unusually dirty or offensive nature",0.67,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Asbestos—Where required to wear protective equipment as required by the appropriate occupational health authority for the handling of materials containing asbestos or working in close proximity to employees handling such materials",0.9,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Bitumen work—Where handling hot bitumen or asphalt or dipping materials in creosote",0.9,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Coloured mortar—Where engaged in the use of coloured additives in mortar",0.79,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Second-hand timber—- Where working with second-hand timber and the employee's tools are damaged by nail, dumps or other foreign matter on the timber - Damage must be immediately reported to their supervisor",2.7,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Lifting—5.5–9kg blocks—- Where required to lift blocks (other than cindrete blocks for plugging purposes) - Employees will not be required to lift blocks in excess of 20kg unless they are provided with a mechanical aid or with an assisting employee",0.67,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Lifting—9–18kg blocks—- Where required to lift blocks (other than cindrete blocks for plugging purposes) - Employees will not be required to lift blocks in excess of 20kg unless they are provided with a mechanical aid or with an assisting employee",1.24,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Lifting—more than 18kg blocks—- Where required to lift blocks (other than cindrete blocks for plugging purposes) - Employees will not be required to lift blocks in excess of 20kg unless they are provided with a mechanical aid or with an assisting employee",1.8,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Roofing repairs—Where engaged in repairs to roofs",0.9,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Computing quantities—Where regularly required to compute or estimate quantities of materials in respect of the work performed by other employees",5.06,"per day or part thereof","C.1.3"],["Certificate—Where the employee holds a scaffolding certificate or rigging certificate and is required to act on that certificate whilst engaged in work requiring a certified person",0.67,"per hour","C.1.3"],["Leading hand—3–10 employees—Where the leading hand is in charge of 3–10 employees",34.16,"per week","C.1.3"],["Leading hand—11–20 employees—Where the leading hand is in charge of 11–20 employees",53.94,"per week","C.1.3"],["Leading hand—more than 20 employees—Where the leading hand is in charge of more than 20 employees",68.55,"per week","C.1.3"],["Explosive power tools—Where required to operate explosive power tools",1.69,"per day","C.1.3"],["Grindstone—Where grindstone or wheel is not made available by the employer",7.19,"per week","C.1.3"],["Relieving officer—Where appointed as a relieving officer (relieves at short notice another security officer, a display roster is not required and 24 hours' notice of shift will be given where possible)",33.04,"per week","C.1.3"]],"ea":[["Overtime meal allowance",21.63,"per occurence","C.2.1"],["Compensation for damage to clothing and personal effects",359.36,"maximum","C.2.2"],["Compensation for tools",1239.0,"maximum","C.2.2"]]}